Final review: <html>
<title>COMX SuperBoard</title>
<body>

<h1>COMX SuperBoard</h1>
<p>
For details about the SuperBoard (SB) project, see the <a href="https://www.comx35.com/superboard.html">COMX SuperBoard</a> page.
</p>

<p>
To run the COMX emulator with the SuperBoard, select the XML file <code>superboard.xml</code> or <code>superboard-80col.xml</code>.
</p>


<h2>Settings</h2>
<p>
To open the SuperBoard Settings window, select <strong>Settings / COMX SuperBoard</strong>. The settings window contains three tabs (1), as described in the following subsections.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/comx_sb_settings.png" border="0" width="644" height="660">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) Settings tabs</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Save All</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
All tabs contain a <strong>Save All</strong> button (2); make sure to press this button to save any changes.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> While running the COMX emulator, no settings can be changed in the <strong>Online</strong> and <strong>USB</strong> tabs. The COMX emulator must be running to delete backup files in the <strong>Backup</strong> tab.
</p>


<h3>Online</h3>
<p>
The <strong>Online</strong> tab shows all settings related to USB commands using online connections, i.e., <code>USB HSWEB</code>, <code>EMAIL</code>, and <code>BROWSER</code>.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/comx_sb_settings_online.png" border="0" width="888" height="660">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Player name</strong> and <strong>Player location</strong> text fields</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Email address</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Home page</strong> text field</li>
<li>(4) <strong>Bookmark</strong> selector and text field</li>
<li>(5) Bookmark <strong>Store</strong> button</li>
<li>(6) <strong>Aliases</strong> selector</li>
<li>(7) <strong>Alias</strong> and <strong>email address</strong> text field</li>
<li>(8) <strong>Delete</strong> button</li>
<li>(9) Aliases <strong>Store</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
Define the <strong>Player name</strong> and <strong>Player location</strong> (1), as used in the <code>USB HSWEB</code> command. The maximum length is 25 characters. The following characters are not allowed and will be ignored: <code># ~ ; :</code>.
</p>

<p>
To use your email address as sender with <code>USB EMAIL</code>, enter a valid email address in the <strong>Email address</strong> field (2).
</p>

<p>
The <strong>Home page</strong> (3) and <strong>Bookmark</strong> (4) fields are used by the <code>USB BROWSER</code> command. These can be accessed on the COMX by pressing <code>H</code> or <code>0-9</code> during a browser session. The maximum length is 126 characters. To store a bookmark, press the <strong>Store</strong> button (5); this button is enabled when text is entered in the <strong>Bookmark</strong> field (4).
</p>

<p>
Email aliases are used by the <code>USB EMAIL</code> command. Existing aliases can be edited using the <strong>Aliases</strong> selector (6). To define a new alias, select <strong>NEW</strong> and enter the alias and email address (7). Press <strong>Store</strong> (9) to save or <strong>Delete</strong> (8) to remove the alias.
</p>


<h3>USB</h3>
<p>
The <strong>USB</strong> tab shows all settings related to USB commands: <code>CD</code>, <code>CHAR</code>, <code>BSAVE</code>, <code>DSAVE</code>, <code>PSAVE</code>, <code>DISKTOIMG</code>, <code>SYSSAVE</code>, and <code>NSAVE</code>.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/comx_sb_settings_usb.png" border="0" width="668" height="660">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Root</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Root path</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Show top directory in USB CD</strong> selector</li>
<li>(4) <strong>Case conversion</strong> field</li>
<li>(5) <strong>Back-up</strong> field</li>
</ul>

<p>
Use the <strong>Root</strong> button (1) or change the path manually (2) to define the root directory visible to the COMX. This is the highest directory level accessible by the COMX.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Show top directory in USB CD</strong> (3) - Select Yes / No:
</p>
<ul>
<li><code>No</code>: PR <code>USB CD</code> shows <code>/</code></li>
<li><code>Yes</code>: PR <code>USB CD</code> shows the root directory (e.g., <code>COMX</code> when using the default root)</li>
</ul>

<p>
<strong>Case conversion</strong> (4) is used only with <code>USB CHAR(0)</code> (default, normal character set) or <code>USB CHAR(1)</code> (lower case). Filenames and directory names are converted to lower case, upper case, or capitalised as specified. When using <code>USB CHAR(2)</code> or <code>USB CHAR(3)</code>, filenames are stored exactly as typed on the COMX.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Back-up</strong> (5) - Select Yes / No:
</p>
<ul>
<li><code>Yes</code>: Creates backup files using format <code>nameNumber.type.bak</code> (e.g., <code>happiehap1.comx.bak</code>)</li>
<li><code>No</code>: COMX prompts for overwrite (<code>Y/N</code>) if the file already exists</li>
</ul>


<h3>Backup</h3>
<p>
The <strong>Backup</strong> tab shows all backup (<code>.bak</code>) files (1) in the selected directory, and optionally, subdirectories (2).
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/comx_sb_settings_backup.png" border="0" width="668" height="660">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Backup files</strong> field</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Include sub directories</strong> checkbox</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Yes</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
Press <strong>Yes</strong> (3) to delete all listed backup files.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> The <strong>Backup</strong> tab is only enabled when the COMX emulator is running.
</p>

</body>
</html>
